      ],
      "title": "NTLMSSP: Domain and Workstation in Negotiate are never Unicode",
      "message": "NTLMSSP: Domain and Workstation in Negotiate are never Unicode\n\nMS-NLMP 2.2.1.1 NEGOTIATE_MESSAGE[1]:\n\n        DomainName ... MUST be encoded using the OEM character set.\n        WorkstationName ... MUST be encoded using the OEM character set.\n\nDavenport document, The Type 1 Message[2]:\n\n        The supplied domain ... is always in OEM format, even if Unicode is supported by the client.\n        The supplied workstation ... too, is in OEM rather than Unicode.\n\nNote too that the flags are known as NTLMSSP_NEGOTIATE_OEM_DOMAIN_SUPPLIED\nand NTLMSSP_NEGOTIATE_OEM_WORKSTATION_SUPPLIED.\n\nThis reverts 19f4af8652ff2d7d254f04bf719174466608e84f and adds a comment\nto try to prevent further accidental \"fixes\".\n\nThis fixes a malformed error in frame 4 of map_cap_interesting.pcap in\n!10193\n\n[1] - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/windows_protocols/ms-nlmp/b34032e5-3aae-4bc6-84c3-c6d80eadf7f2\n[2] - https://davenport.sourceforge.net/ntlm.html#theType1Message\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
